      "F12": "The absence of abnormal vascular structures and suggestion of a lipomatous process on CT scan is highly suggestive of lipofibromatous hamartoma.",
      "F3": "The finger being larger than the others since birth and growing progressively is a key characteristic of macrodactyly, but also seen in other conditions like lipofibromatous hamartoma and Proteus syndrome.",
      "F6": "The middle finger being enlarged but with normal overlying skin is consistent with macrodactyly and lipofibromatous hamartoma, but less specific for other conditions."
